    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, the sole test class `AcceptanceTest` passes).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe membership level was computed by an inline MapStruct expression capped at `Math.min(3, \u2026)` \u2014 there was no level 4 at all. I introduced level 4 gated on tenure while keeping structural impact low:\n\n1. **New helper** `rest/function/owner/MembershipLevel.java` \u2014 a small, cohesive unit (mirroring the existing `AgeBand`/`HouseholdTier` helpers) with zero surrounding class context. It computes the base factors (email on file, no namesake) toward 3, adds a 4th level only when `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, now) > 365`, and caps at `Math.min(4, \u2026)`. Uses `LocalDate.now()`, consistent with `BulkSignup`/`RejectFutureRegistrationDate`.\n\n2. **One-line edit** to `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 the `membershipLevel` expression now just calls `MembershipLevel.of(owner)`, replacing the complex inline ternary.\n\nBecause a new owner's `registrationDate` is set to today (`BuildOwner`), its tenure is 0, so the tenure factor never fires \u2014 a new owner with an email, `namesakeCount` 0, and a 3-member household lands at **3, not 4**, exactly as the spec and the new `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` test require.\n\nI deliberately left `HouseholdTier` untouched (avoiding a third touched file and edits to an existing method), since the spec and tests only constrain the new-owner cap and the tenure gate.",
